{title: Down in the Valley}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 92}
{meta: public_domain Traditional American folk song from Kentucky, collected in the early 20th century.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Down in the valley, the [G]valley so [D]low,[D]
[D]Hang your head over, hear the [D]wind [G]blow.[G]
[G]Hear the wind blow, dear, [G]hear the wind [D]blow,[D]
[D]Hang your head over, hear the [D]wind [G]blow.[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Roses love sunshine, [G]violets love [D]dew,[D]
[D]Angels in heaven know [D]I love [G]you.[G]
[G]Know I love you, dear, [G]know I love [D]you,[D]
[D]Angels in heaven know [D]I love [G]you.[G]
{end_of_verse}
